      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "We studied the feasibility of using the impedance frequency curve method (IFM) to detect the myocardial physical heterogeneity of a cross-circulated isolated canine left ventricle with regional ischemia. The curve changed from a single-peak configuration to a double-peak configuration after the LAD coronary flow cessation and returned to the single-peak configuration with the reperfusion of LAD coronary flow. We concluded that IFM can be a useful tool to describe the physical heterogeneity of the ventricular muscle under the regional ischemia."},
